          "issue": "The main text defensibly carries the evil one forward as the subject, but the disclosure is incomplete. The source note mentions possible influence from ὕλη on γέγονεν and συμβέβηκεν without clearly preserving the alternative that the following predications, including ἐστίν and αἰεὶ ἦν, concern the matter. It also asserts that the contextual choice is defensible without explaining why that grouping was selected.",
          "suggested_revision": "Expand the source-quoted note to state explicitly that an alternative grouping concerns the origin and status of the matter from which the evil one arose, including whether that matter belongs among relative or dependent things or always existed. Explain the main text's decision to carry forward the evil one as subject from ὅθεν γέγονεν and the surrounding inquiry into his origin. This is an interpretive disclosure issue, not evidence of defective or unverified print.",
